From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:37:37 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] kboot: hand the speaker amps' configuration from the
 ADT to the kernel

The kernel's SN012776 driver programs every amp's brownout prevention
block from a copy typed into the driver, and nothing tells it how macOS
sets the amps' DC blocker. Both come from the ADT: the node of each
amp group's first amp ("audio-control,sn012776", with speakerN phandles
to the others) carries the group's configuration, which macOS applies
to every amp of the group.

Copy that node's bop-config and amp-dcblocker-config, byte for byte,
to every amp of the group in the DT, as apple,bop-config and
apple,amp-dcblocker-config. A property the group lacks is removed from
its amps, so the kernel never sees a value that did not come from the
Mac. Amps are matched to the DT's ti,sn012776 nodes by I2C address,
which must name exactly one node; a group with an amp that cannot be
matched is left alone, so the kernel gets all of a group's
configuration or none of it. Nothing in this pass stops the boot.

Tests: tests/run-kboot-audio.sh builds kboot_audio.c with aura's own ADT
reader and libfdt for the host and runs seven synthetic scenarios (a
three-amp group over two buses, a group without a DC blocker setting
and a stale DT copy, a single amp, an amp missing from the DT, an
ambiguous address, a dangling phandle, no amps). Given a Mac's
IODeviceTree plist and kernel DTB it prints what the kernel would get:
on the M1 Pro (J316s), M2 (J413) and M4 Pro (J616s) ADTs every amp gets
a brownout block identical to the one the kernel driver carries today,
the J413 and J616s amps get their DC blocker setting and the J316s
amps, whose ADT has none, get none.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>

(cherry picked from aurora-silicon/aura commit 13c4f7a934c203f05cfd98e62b12a7ec66871159;
 Makefile and kboot.c context adjusted to omacom m1n1)
